<title>SWEDEN: FORECAST-Handelsbanken sees Sweden 97 GDP 2.2 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Handelsbanken sees Sweden 97 GDP 2.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commecial Swedish bank Handelsbanken issued the following forecasts on Monday for the Swedish economy;</p>
<p> (pct change unless otherwise stated)     1996    1997    1998</p>
<p> Gross Domestic Product			  1.7     2.2     2.2</p>
<p> Consumer price index (yr/yr)		  1.2     1.7     2.2</p>
<p> Unemployment rate				 7.9     7.7     7.4</p>
<p> Private spending				  1.3     1.9     2.0</p>
<p> Public spending				  -1.5    -0.7    -0.8</p>
<p> Gross investments				10.0     2.4     1.5</p>
<p> Stockbuilding				    -1.3     0.4     0.1</p>
<p> Exports					     6.3     7.0     8.0</p>
<p> Imports					     3.9     6.7     6.9</p>
<p> Industrial production			   2.8     5.5     5.0</p>
<p> Wage increases, total economy		 5.0     4.4     3.5</p>
<p> Wage increases, manufacturing		 6.2     5.0     3.5</p>
<p> State borrowing reqmt (blns crowns)	50	40	15</p>
<p>  &quot;	 &quot;	 &quot;    (as pct of GDP)     3.0     2.2     0.8</p>
<p>-- Paul de Bendern, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1006</p>
</text>
